# UI

Read `docs/design-language.md` before changing a screen. That file holds the tokens. Screen files in `docs/design/screens/` win for layout. `docs/design-language.md` wins for tokens.

- Use only colors, type, and motion named there. If a value is missing, add it to the doc after the user chooses it. Do not ship an invented palette as the brand.
- Black mark on light grounds. White mark on black grounds. Do not recolor, stretch, or add effects to the logo.
- Glow is only the named files `glow-dark.jpg` and `glow-light.jpg`, and only where a screen places them. After the intro, do not add stars, nebulae, decorative gradients, or neon.
- Mobile and desktop are both real layouts. Reference widths are 390px and 1440px. Same tasks. Build them fluid.
- `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` skips the intro to its final state: mark, wordmark, and Enter. Write that with Tailwind's `motion-reduce:` variant.
- Checkout is Shopify's page. Do not rebuild it.
- Style with Tailwind utility classes, as decided in `docs/architecture.md`. The Tailwind entry file is the only handwritten CSS. Do not add a CSS module or a per-component stylesheet.
- `docs/design-language.md` and the accepted requirement win over `design-taste-frontend` and over any third-party `DESIGN.md`.

```tsx
// Wrong: an unnamed palette treated as final
<button className="bg-[#111111] font-[Neue Haas Grotesk]">Add</button>

// Right: a token that already exists in docs/design-language.md
<button className="bg-text text-bg motion-reduce:transition-none">Add</button>
```
